# Retention for the syslog-proxy local log copy (/opt/d2-edge/syslog-proxy/logs).
#
# These files are a byte-for-byte duplicate of what syslog-ng has already
# shipped to Graylog (10.255.255.20:12203) — the d_local and d_graylog
# destinations sit on the same log{} statement, so their processed counters
# advance in lockstep. Graylog is the system of record; the local tree is a
# short-window convenience for on-Pi troubleshooting only.
#
# Nothing purged it before this file existed, so the tree grew ~1.3 GB/day
# indefinitely. Observed on ncm001-bc-pi01 2026-07-20: 36 GB of a 58 GB card.
#
# 7 days matches what has run on d2001-nw-pi01 since 2026-04-13.
# Deletes files first, then prunes the empty dated directories they leave.
0 4 * * * root find /opt/d2-edge/syslog-proxy/logs/ -type f -mtime +7 -delete 2>/dev/null; find /opt/d2-edge/syslog-proxy/logs/ -mindepth 1 -type d -empty -delete 2>/dev/null
